  "boxes": [
    {
      "type": "anchorbox",
      "title": "The Art of Listening",
      "description": "He is praised for being exceptionally eager to listen (Sunibe ko Rasiya). In the *Valmiki Ramayana* (*Kishkindha Kanda, 3:28-33*), Lord Rama notes that Hanuman's flawless speech is proof of his highly disciplined, attentive listening as a student of the Vedas. True mastery in communication and leadership begins with the patient, active absorption of knowledge.",
      "motivating_text": "",
      "citation": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "gotchabox",
      "items": [
        "Consonant Melt (लक्ष्मण → लखन): The harsh consonant cluster `kshma` (क्ष्म) in Sanskrit melts down into the softer, breathy `kha` (ख) in Awadhi, making it much easier to sing! The Gita Press version uses लषन instead of लखन. Both carry the same metrical value.",
        "The व → ब Shift (बसिया): The Sanskrit root for dwelling is वस् (Vas). True to form, the Awadhi immediately hardens that initial v into a b, giving us बसिया (Basiyaa)."
      ]
    }
  ]
